OwnGit {{.Version}} macOS prototype

This unsigned local prototype is not a public release. It has no
publisher-signed app or DMG and has not been notarized or installed through a
completed native acceptance run. An ad hoc signature added to a Mach-O file by
Apple's linker is not a publisher signature.

Install
  Copy OwnGit.app to your own ~/Applications folder with Finder. Installation
  does not start OwnGit or add a Login Item.

Start and stop
  Open OwnGit.app manually. The app starts the bundled OwnGit server with
  browser opening enabled. Before setup is complete, it opens the private
  setup file. After setup, it opens the dashboard after the server starts. Use
  Quit OwnGit from the application menu to request a graceful stop.

Upgrade
  Quit OwnGit, retain the previous verified app until the new build starts,
  and replace OwnGit.app. Replacing the app does not remove state or
  repositories. An older app is not promised to read state after a completed
  schema migration.

Remove
  Quit OwnGit and move OwnGit.app to Trash. Remove a Login Item separately if
  you created one. State and repositories are retained.

Requirements
  Git must already be installed. Pull request merge requires Git 2.38 or newer.

Coding tool integration
  OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md
  OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/integrations/skills/owngit-checks/SKILL.md
  Copy the skill yourself if you want a coding tool to load it. The helper
  binary is at OwnGit.app/Contents/Resources/bin/owngit and is not on PATH.

Public readiness
  Public distribution additionally requires an authorized Developer ID
  signature, hardened runtime, notarization, stapling, and observed Gatekeeper
  behavior. No protection should be bypassed to run this prototype.
